{"ts":"2026-07-26T22:37:23.410Z","author":"harness:opencode","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"opencode","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-hipfu9"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Recurring reminders: a standing check (daily release-health, weekly governance sweep) re-arms itself on fire instead of requiring manual re-scheduling"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reminders are single-fire (at=...,text=... only); events already expand recurrence (pm-vg5h) but reminders do not. A standing operational check such as pm-7zs0 (daily auto-release verification) must be re-scheduled by hand after every fire, which means the safety net silently disappears the first time the re-schedule is forgotten. Add an opt-in recurrence field to the reminder facet (cadence + next-fire derivation, re-arm recorded as a history mutation), consistent with the calendar recurrence model and the builtin-calendar package boundary (pm-o3fh). Horizon: near-mid; small surface, high operational value."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","calendar","horizon:mid","recurrence","release","reminders"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-26T22:37:23.410Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T22:37:23.410Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:opencode"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a1f80d4c7d62ac25e621034c20b3539dbd9e9b5a419342f02c0a0fd7eaa3fa53","message":""}
